{% comment %}
  Walterin · Walter desert. Scroll-driven: the scrollbar is the motor, nothing plays on its own.

  Ported from _prototype/walter-desert-reference_1.html ("A · Pinned run"). The desert outline and
  the sun are the prototype's hand-drawn coordinates, copied character for character — they are
  traced art, not geometry, so re-rounding them would flatten the wobble that makes them read as
  drawn. The prototype's label bar, intro and notes were review chrome and are not here.

  The desert is ONE path. Its fill is the sand and its top edge is the only ground line, so there
  can never be a colour step between the pyramids and the sand in front of them. Its closing corners
  are pushed to y=980, well below the 620 viewBox, so the stroke that would otherwise run along the
  bottom of the frame is clipped away and the top edge is the only line you see.

  Verifying that the loop sleeps: the rAF loop writes data-wui-desert-running="true" on the root
  while it owns a frame and "false" the moment the IntersectionObserver says the section has left
  the viewport. Poll that attribute to prove the scene costs nothing off-screen. It stays "false"
  under prefers-reduced-motion, where no loop is ever started.
{% endcomment %}
{%- liquid
  assign walter = section.settings.walter
  comment
    The fallback is the theme asset, so the section renders the moment it is dropped on a page and
    before anyone opens the picker.
  endcomment
  assign walter_w = 227
  assign walter_h = 243
  assign walter_src = 'walter-skate.png' | asset_url
  if walter != blank
    assign walter_w = walter.width
    assign walter_h = walter.height
    assign walter_src = walter | image_url: width: 480
  endif
  assign walter_alt = walter.alt | default: 'Walter on a skateboard'
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  A fixed id, not Shopify's generated one, so the inline script below finds its own instance even
  when the section is added twice to one page.
{%- endcomment -%}
<div
  class="wui-desert"
  id="wui-desert-{{ section.id }}"
  data-wui-desert
  data-wui-desert-running="false"
  style="
    --wd-h: {{ section.settings.section_height }};
    --wd-walter: {{ section.settings.walter_size }};
    --wd-sun: {{ section.settings.sun_size }};
    --wd-sun-x: {{ section.settings.sun_x }}%;
    --wd-sun-y: {{ section.settings.sun_y }}%;
    --wd-sky-top: {{ section.settings.sky_top }};
    --wd-sky-low: {{ section.settings.sky_low }};
    --wd-sand: {{ section.settings.sand }};
    --wd-ink: {{ section.settings.outline }};
  "
>
  <div class="wui-desert__pin" data-wui-desert-pin>
    <div class="wui-desert__stage">
      {%- if section.settings.show_sun -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Behind the pyramids (z-index 0) and low in the sky, so it reads as morning rather than
          noon. A square box with a centred r=40 circle keeps it a true circle at every size.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <svg class="wui-desert__sun" viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
          <circle cx="50" cy="50" r="40" stroke-width="3.6" vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke"/>
        </svg>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        preserveAspectRatio="none" lets the drawing fill a frame far wider than it was drawn in. The
        price is that a narrow screen stretches the peaks upwards, which is why the drawing is made
        wider than 2× below 1100px — see the media queries.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <svg
        class="wui-desert__sand"
        viewBox="0 0 1200 620"
        preserveAspectRatio="none"
        aria-hidden="true"
        focusable="false"
        data-wui-desert-sand
      >
        <path d="M -40.9 238.2 Q -24.8 227.8 -17.8 223.5 Q -10.9 219.3 -4.9 214.7 Q 1.0 210.0 8.2 204.8 Q 15.4 199.7 22.7 193.8 Q 30.0 187.9 38.1 184.8 Q 46.3 181.7 52.7 175.1 Q 59.2 168.6 67.7 165.4 Q 76.2 162.3 83.3 155.9 Q 90.4 149.5 97.9 155.0 Q 105.3 160.5 111.5 167.6 Q 117.6 174.6 122.1 180.6 Q 126.7 186.6 133.6 194.8 Q 140.4 203.1 146.5 208.9 Q 152.6 214.7 160.2 220.6 Q 167.9 226.5 174.1 232.1 Q 180.2 237.7 184.4 231.6 Q 188.6 225.4 195.7 219.4 Q 202.8 213.4 207.3 207.3 Q 211.8 201.2 217.6 193.9 Q 223.4 186.6 229.7 181.1 Q 236.1 175.6 240.1 168.7 Q 244.1 161.8 250.3 156.1 Q 256.5 150.3 262.5 142.2 Q 268.5 134.2 274.6 127.2 Q 280.7 120.2 284.7 115.3 Q 288.7 110.4 293.4 103.2 Q 298.2 95.9 303.3 102.4 Q 308.4 108.9 315.7 114.6 Q 323.0 120.4 328.7 125.7 Q 334.5 131.0 339.4 137.8 Q 344.3 144.5 349.5 150.1 Q 354.6 155.8 360.7 163.0 Q 366.8 170.3 371.2 175.6 Q 375.7 180.9 380.0 187.0 Q 384.4 193.0 391.3 199.8 Q 398.3 206.6 404.1 210.7 Q 410.0 214.9 414.3 221.9 Q 418.6 228.9 423.0 234.3 Q 427.5 239.8 434.3 233.9 Q 441.1 228.0 447.3 224.7 Q 453.4 221.4 460.0 215.0 Q 466.6 208.7 473.8 205.3 Q 480.9 201.9 486.5 195.8 Q 492.1 189.7 499.8 185.9 Q 507.4 182.0 514.5 176.9 Q 521.7 171.9 526.9 176.6 Q 532.2 181.2 539.1 188.3 Q 545.9 195.3 554.2 199.3 Q 562.4 203.2 567.0 209.2 Q 571.6 215.3 578.5 221.8 Q 585.3 228.3 592.9 233.5 Q 600.5 238.8 604.3 233.2 Q 608.1 227.6 614.4 222.0 Q 620.7 216.3 627.5 210.7 Q 634.4 205.0 638.6 198.8 Q 642.7 192.6 648.5 185.1 Q 654.2 177.7 660.2 173.6 Q 666.1 169.5 671.3 163.5 Q 676.6 157.5 680.7 150.5 Q 684.8 143.5 689.4 138.1 Q 693.9 132.7 699.2 125.2 Q 704.4 117.8 710.1 112.0 Q 715.8 106.2 721.5 100.0 Q 727.2 93.7 731.6 87.9 Q 736.1 82.2 741.7 76.7 Q 747.3 71.3 752.4 66.6 Q 757.5 61.9 764.7 66.1 Q 771.9 70.2 776.7 76.7 Q 781.4 83.2 787.3 88.6 Q 793.3 94.0 800.2 102.3 Q 807.1 110.6 811.8 115.2 Q 816.5 119.9 821.2 124.9 Q 825.8 129.9 832.2 136.4 Q 838.5 142.8 845.4 148.5 Q 852.4 154.2 855.9 162.3 Q 859.5 170.3 866.5 174.3 Q 873.5 178.2 879.2 183.9 Q 884.9 189.5 890.5 198.0 Q 896.1 206.5 902.7 211.8 Q 909.2 217.0 913.3 222.2 Q 917.4 227.3 922.8 234.4 Q 928.3 241.4 934.2 235.2 Q 940.2 229.0 944.6 221.3 Q 949.1 213.6 955.4 209.3 Q 961.6 205.0 966.7 198.3 Q 971.8 191.6 976.7 185.2 Q 981.7 178.7 985.1 171.9 Q 988.6 165.1 993.9 157.6 Q 999.2 150.1 1003.4 144.5 Q 1007.5 138.9 1013.1 146.2 Q 1018.7 153.5 1025.6 159.1 Q 1032.4 164.7 1037.3 172.4 Q 1042.3 180.0 1047.3 184.7 Q 1052.4 189.3 1055.5 195.2 Q 1058.5 201.1 1063.5 207.3 Q 1068.4 213.5 1074.5 221.5 Q 1080.6 229.6 1086.2 234.7 Q 1091.8 239.9 1099.6 238.8 Q 1107.5 237.7 1114.3 235.4 Q 1121.2 233.1 1131.7 231.4 Q 1142.1 229.8 1150.0 227.1 Q 1158.0 224.3 1164.8 223.2 Q 1171.7 222.1 1180.4 220.1 Q 1189.1 218.2 1199.1 215.2 Q 1209.1 212.2 1216.0 211.7 Q 1222.8 211.2 1231.4 208.1 T 1240.0 205.0 L 1240 980 L -40 980 Z" stroke-width="3.6" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-linecap="round" vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke"/>
      </svg>

      {%- if section.settings.show_tracks -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          No viewBox: the track user units are CSS pixels, so the JS can hand it the same numbers it
          uses for Walter. The gradient is painted on the stroke and runs to zero opacity at its own
          left end, so each track dies out instead of stopping at an edge.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <svg class="wui-desert__tracks" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
          <defs>
            <linearGradient id="wui-desert-fade-{{ section.id }}" x1="0" y1="0" x2="1" y2="0">
              <stop offset="0" stop-opacity="0"/>
              <stop offset=".45" stop-opacity=".1"/>
              <stop offset=".85" stop-opacity=".3"/>
              <stop offset="1" stop-opacity=".38"/>
            </linearGradient>
          </defs>
          <path d="" stroke="url(#wui-desert-fade-{{ section.id }})" data-wui-desert-track-low />
          <path d="" stroke="url(#wui-desert-fade-{{ section.id }})" data-wui-desert-track-high />
        </svg>
      {%- endif -%}

      <div class="wui-desert__walter" data-wui-desert-walter>
        <img
          src="{{ walter_src }}"
          alt="{{ walter_alt | escape }}"
          width="{{ walter_w }}"
          height="{{ walter_h }}"
          loading="eager"
        >
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

{%- comment -%}
  Parsed before the first paint, on purpose. Without JavaScript Walter is parked at 15% so the scene
  is never empty; the attribute below switches him to the scroll-driven origin, and setting it here
  rather than in a deferred bundle is what stops the parked position flashing on load.
{%- endcomment -%}
<script>
  (function () {
    var root = document.getElementById('wui-desert-{{ section.id }}');
    if (!root) return;

    /* Reduced motion keeps the parked position and never starts a loop. */
    var reduce = window.matchMedia && matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
    if (reduce) return;
    root.setAttribute('data-wui-desert-js', 'true');

    var pin = root.querySelector('[data-wui-desert-pin]');
    var sand = root.querySelector('[data-wui-desert-sand]');
    var walter = root.querySelector('[data-wui-desert-walter]');
    var low = root.querySelector('[data-wui-desert-track-low]');
    var high = root.querySelector('[data-wui-desert-track-high]');

    var START = {{ section.settings.start_x | json }};
    var END = {{ section.settings.end_x | json }};

    /* Verbatim from the prototype: 12% of the drawing, which is 2× the stage, so the desert covers
       roughly a quarter of the screen while Walter covers 1.4 screens. That ratio is the depth. */
    var DRIFT = 12;
    var BOB = 4;
    var TILT = 2.5;

    /* Where the board touches the sand, as a fraction of the stage height. Walter's CSS bottom is
       derived from the same --wd-ground, so the two can never drift apart.
       The drawn ridge undulates between roughly 47% and 55% of the stage, so one flat contact line
       below all of it keeps him in the near sand instead of climbing a pyramid. */
    var ground = 0.58;

    /* Measured as the front and rear wheels of assets/walter-skate.png (227px wide): the lowest
       opaque pixels sit at x≈190 and x≈123. */
    var FRONT = 0.845;
    var REAR = 0.6;

    var raf = 0;
    var inView = false;
    var W = 0;
    var H = 0;
    var aw = 150;

    function clamp(v, a, b) { return v < a ? a : (v > b ? b : v); }

    /* Two sines of different wavelengths: the long one is the arc of the turn, the short one the
       chatter of a hard wheel on sand. */
    function trackPath(x0, x1, y, amp) {
      var d = '';
      var n = Math.max(2, Math.round((x1 - x0) / 26));
      for (var i = 0; i <= n; i++) {
        var x = x0 + (x1 - x0) * i / n;
        var yy = y + Math.sin(x / 34) * amp + Math.sin(x / 11) * (amp * 0.35);
        d += (i ? ' L ' : 'M ') + x.toFixed(1) + ' ' + yy.toFixed(1);
      }
      return d;
    }

    /* Every layout read the scene needs, in one place, called on entry and on resize only. */
    function measure() {
      W = pin.offsetWidth;
      H = pin.offsetHeight;
      aw = walter.offsetWidth || 150;
      var g = parseFloat(getComputedStyle(root).getPropertyValue('--wd-ground'));
      if (!isNaN(g)) ground = g / 100;
    }

    function frame() {
      /* The only per-frame layout read. window.innerHeight is a cached value, not a reflow. */
      var r = root.getBoundingClientRect();
      var p = clamp(-r.top / ((r.height - window.innerHeight) || 1), 0, 1);

      var x = (START + p * (END - START)) / 100 * W;
      var bob = Math.sin(p * Math.PI * 7) * BOB;
      var tilt = Math.sin(p * Math.PI * 5) * TILT;
      walter.style.transform =
        'translate3d(' + x.toFixed(2) + 'px,' + bob.toFixed(2) + 'px,0) rotate(' + tilt.toFixed(2) + 'deg)';
      sand.style.transform = 'translate3d(' + (-p * DRIFT).toFixed(3) + '%,0,0)';

      if (low) {
        var gy = H * ground;
        /* A quarter of the screen at most, and shorter still on a phone, where a long track would
           reach the opposite edge before it had faded. */
        var len = Math.min(250, W * 0.24);
        var fx = x + aw * FRONT;
        var rx = x + aw * REAR;
        low.setAttribute('d', trackPath(Math.max(-30, fx - len), fx, gy, 1));
        /* 7px nearer the horizon and starting further back: the pair of wheels on the far side. */
        high.setAttribute('d', trackPath(Math.max(-30, rx - len * 0.8), rx, gy - 7, 0.8));
      }

      raf = requestAnimationFrame(frame);
    }

    function start() {
      if (raf) return;
      measure();
      root.setAttribute('data-wui-desert-running', 'true');
      raf = requestAnimationFrame(frame);
    }

    function stop() {
      if (raf) cancelAnimationFrame(raf);
      raf = 0;
      root.setAttribute('data-wui-desert-running', 'false');
    }

    var io = new IntersectionObserver(function (entries) {
      inView = entries[entries.length - 1].isIntersecting;
      if (inView) start(); else stop();
    });
    io.observe(root);

    /* iOS Safari throttles observer callbacks during a momentum fling, which would leave the scene
       frozen for the length of it. A scroll event is the cheap way back in. */
    addEventListener('scroll', function () { if (inView && !raf) start(); }, { passive: true });

    var pending = 0;
    addEventListener('resize', function () {
      if (pending) return;
      pending = requestAnimationFrame(function () { pending = 0; measure(); });
    }, { passive: true });

    /* The theme editor re-renders a section without reloading the page: let go of the old one. */
    document.addEventListener('shopify:section:unload', function (e) {
      if (e.detail && e.detail.sectionId === {{ section.id | json }}) { stop(); io.disconnect(); }
    });
  })();
</script>

{% stylesheet %}
/* Walterin · Walter desert. Self-contained: it has no text, so it borrows no type or spacing tokens
   and works on a page template whether or not the body carries .wui. */
.wui-desert {
  --wd-w: calc(var(--wd-walter) * 1px);
  --wd-sun-px: calc(var(--wd-sun) * 1px);
  /* The contact line, read back by the JS so the tracks start where the wheels are. */
  --wd-ground: 58%;
  /* assets/walter-skate.png carries 3px of transparent space under the wheels at its own 227px
     width. Expressed as a fraction of his rendered width it holds at every breakpoint, so the
     wheels sit on the line instead of hovering over it. */
  --wd-sink: calc(var(--wd-w) * 0.0132);
  position: relative;
  height: calc(var(--wd-h) * 1vh);
}

/* The scene holds still while the page scrolls past it. svh, not vh, so the mobile toolbar
   collapsing does not resize the stage mid-run. */
.wui-desert__pin {
  position: sticky;
  top: 0;
  height: 100svh;
  min-height: 420px;
}

.wui-desert__stage {
  position: relative;
  height: 100%;
  overflow: hidden;
  /* The bare 46% is a colour-interpolation hint, not a stop: it moves the halfway blend down the
     sky without naming a third colour, which keeps the setting panel at the two the sky needs. */
  background: linear-gradient(var(--wd-sky-top) 0%, 46%, var(--wd-sky-low) 58%, var(--wd-sky-low) 100%);
}

.wui-desert__sun {
  position: absolute;
  z-index: 0;
  left: var(--wd-sun-x);
  bottom: var(--wd-sun-y);
  width: var(--wd-sun-px);
  height: var(--wd-sun-px);
  opacity: .95;
}
.wui-desert__sun circle { fill: #FCE206; stroke: var(--wd-ink); }

.wui-desert__sand {
  position: absolute;
  z-index: 1;
  left: 0;
  bottom: 0;
  width: 200%;
  height: 72.3%;
  will-change: transform;
}
.wui-desert__sand path { fill: var(--wd-sand); stroke: var(--wd-ink); }

.wui-desert__tracks {
  position: absolute;
  z-index: 2;
  inset: 0;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  pointer-events: none;
}
.wui-desert__tracks path { fill: none; stroke-width: 2.6; stroke-linecap: round; }
.wui-desert__tracks stop { stop-color: var(--wd-ink); }

.wui-desert__walter {
  position: absolute;
  z-index: 3;
  /* Parked where someone without JavaScript still meets him. The attribute below hands him over to
     the scroll. */
  left: 15%;
  bottom: calc(100% - var(--wd-ground) - var(--wd-sink));
  width: var(--wd-w);
  transform-origin: 50% 100%;
  will-change: transform;
  pointer-events: none;
}
.wui-desert[data-wui-desert-js='true'] .wui-desert__walter { left: 0; }
/* width + height on the img and height:auto here: the aspect ratio is known before the file
   arrives, so nothing below the scene moves when it does. */
.wui-desert__walter img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; }

/* 761-1100: a tablet, not a narrow desk. The run is shortened because the same 300vh at 1024 wide
   is a longer hold for a shorter crossing, and the drawing is widened because at this aspect
   preserveAspectRatio="none" has started to stretch the peaks upwards. */
@media (min-width: 761px) and (max-width: 1100px) {
  .wui-desert { height: calc(var(--wd-h) * 0.87vh); --wd-w: calc(var(--wd-walter) * 0.853px); }
  .wui-desert__sand { width: 260%; }
}

@media (max-width: 760px) {
  .wui-desert {
    height: calc(var(--wd-h) * 0.733vh);
    --wd-w: calc(var(--wd-walter) * 0.733px);
    --wd-sun-px: calc(var(--wd-sun) * 0.636px);
  }
  .wui-desert__sand { width: 360%; }
}

/* No loop, no dead space: the wrapper collapses to the one screen the scene occupies, so there is
   nothing left to scroll through, and Walter stays parked and still. */
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  .wui-desert { height: auto; }
  .wui-desert__pin { position: static; }
  .wui-desert__walter { left: 15%; transform: none; }
}
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Walter desert",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "wui-section",
  "enabled_on": { "templates": ["page"] },
  "settings": [
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "walter", "label": "Walter", "info": "A transparent PNG facing right. Falls back to walter-skate.png." },
    { "type": "range", "id": "walter_size", "label": "Walter width", "min": 90, "max": 240, "step": 2, "unit": "px", "default": 150, "info": "Desktop. Tablet and phone scale from this (128px and 110px at the default)." },
    { "type": "range", "id": "section_height", "label": "Scroll length", "min": 150, "max": 400, "step": 10, "unit": "vh", "default": 300, "info": "Desktop. Tablet and phone scale from this (260vh and 220vh at the default)." },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Colours" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "sky_top", "label": "Sky, top", "default": "#EFEADC" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "sky_low", "label": "Sky, at the horizon", "default": "#FBE3AE" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "sand", "label": "Sand", "default": "#F5BC42" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "outline", "label": "Outline", "default": "#1C1C1C" },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Sun" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_sun", "label": "Show the sun", "default": true },
    { "type": "range", "id": "sun_size", "label": "Size", "min": 80, "max": 320, "step": 4, "unit": "px", "default": 220 },
    { "type": "range", "id": "sun_x", "label": "From the left", "min": 0, "max": 100, "step": 1, "unit": "%", "default": 49 },
    { "type": "range", "id": "sun_y", "label": "From the bottom", "min": 0, "max": 100, "step": 1, "unit": "%", "default": 48 },

    { "type": "header", "content": "The crossing" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_tracks", "label": "Show the wheel tracks", "default": true },
    { "type": "range", "id": "start_x", "label": "Starts at", "min": -60, "max": 40, "step": 2, "unit": "%", "default": -20, "info": "Of the section width. Below 0 he begins off the left edge." },
    { "type": "range", "id": "end_x", "label": "Ends at", "min": 60, "max": 200, "step": 2, "unit": "%", "default": 118, "info": "Above 100 he leaves past the right edge." }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Walter desert" }]
}
{% endschema %}
